WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.385
"How Well Do Medicines Like Fosamax Work
to Treat Osteoporosis?"

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.600
Drug therapy for osteoporosis

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.340
is recommended
for those 50 and older

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.440
with a history of past hip
or spine fractures,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.600
those with hip or spine
"T-scores"

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.160
of negative 2.5 or less,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.860
and postmenopausal women
or men 50 and older

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.360
who don't make that cut-off

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.520
but have an estimated
20 percent or higher risk

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.980
of a major osteoporotic fracture
over the subsequent decade,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.140
or an estimated
3 percent or greater risk

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.640
of hip fracture, specifically.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.420
A T-score is a measure
of how dense your bones are

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.580
compared to
a 30-year-old white woman.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.860
Since that's the standard,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.660
and we tend to lose bone
as we age,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.300
you can be labeled
as having osteoporosis

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.360
even if you have completely
normal bone density

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:48.960
for your age.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.780
Of course, just because your
bone density may be normal

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.000
doesn't mean
it's necessarily optimal,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.400
which is why the National
Osteoporosis Foundation

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.620
set out these guidelines
for drug treatment.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.560
Though another reason, perhaps,

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.600
is because it gets
substantial funding

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.800
from the drug industry,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.740
which rakes in literally
billions of dollars in profits

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.120
from osteoporosis drugs.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.600
What does the science say?

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.960
The primary drug class
used to treat osteoporosis

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.340
is the bisphosphonates,

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.260
sold as such brands as Fosamax,
Actonel, Boniva, and Reclast.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.440
They are most effective at
reducing vertebral fractures,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.360
cutting the risk
in postmenopausal women

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.760
from 2.8 percent
down to 1.4 percent.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.330
That's a relative risk
reduction of 50 percent,

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.120
but an absolute risk
reduction of only 1.4 percent,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.240
meaning you'd have to treat
71 women to prevent

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.460
just one woman from getting
a vertebral fracture.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.640
Unfortunately, the diagnosis
of vertebral fracture

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.080
is kind of wishy-washy.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.660
Depending on how you define
the changes on x-ray,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.760
the prevalence
of vertebral fractures

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.840
can vary as much as
3 percent to 90 percent

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.700
in the same elderly population--

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.860
almost none to almost all.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.160
They're also poorly predictive
of back pain or disability.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.280
Vertebral fractures can
certainly lead to back pain

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.480
and reduced physical function,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.940
but only about a third
are symptomatic at all.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.300
The most harmful fractures
are hip fractures.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.940
Despite most
of the clinical trials

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.140
for osteoporosis treatment

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.120
being funded by the drug
companies themselves,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.480
no primary prevention benefit
from bisphosphonates

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.160
has been found
for hip fractures.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.080
In other words,
taking these drugs

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.800
has not been convincingly shown
to prevent fracturing your hip

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.640
in the first place.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.340
However, having a prior fracture

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.200
doubles your risk
of breaking another bone,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.900
so, for those at high risk,
bisphosphonate drugs

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.480
may decrease the odds
of hip fracture by 25 percent,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.760
though the absolute
risk reduction is, again,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.720
only about 1 percent.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.420
It may take treating 91 people
for three years

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.860
to prevent one hip fracture.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.400
An overconfidence in the power
of pills and procedures

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.420
for disease prevention

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.760
may be one of the reasons
doctors and patients alike

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.520
may undervalue diet
and lifestyle approaches.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.720
In this study,

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.180
patients were asked to estimate
the number of fractures

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.880
or deaths prevented
in a group of 5,000 patients

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.260
undergoing each
drug intervention

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.820
over a period of 10 years.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.440
The vast majority of people
tended to wildly overestimate

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.540
the ability of mammograms
and colonoscopies

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.620
to prevent cancer deaths,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.860
the power of drugs like Fosamax
to prevent hip fractures,

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.560
and drugs like Lipitor
to prevent fatal heart attacks.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.280
No wonder most people continue
to rely on drugs to save them.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.680
But the dirty little secret is

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.200
that most people said
they wouldn't be willing

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.460
to take many of these drugs

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.120
if they knew how little benefit
these products actually offered.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.700
In a study of those undergoing
bone density scans,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.500
the average five-year
fracture risk

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.000
that would motivate
most participants

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.520
to consider preventative
medicine was 50 to 60 percent,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.220
much higher
than their actual risk.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.740
Most patients want
to be told the truth.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.720
They want to be told
what the chances are

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.400
that the drugs will
actually benefit them,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.760
but there is a tension between
the patient's right to know

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.160
and the likely reduction
in their willingness

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.920
to take the drug
if they knew the truth.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.920
In the bone density scan survey,

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.840
participants
greatly overestimated

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.400
their own personal risk
for hip fracture,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.900
thinking it was
around 19 percent

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.800
over the next 5 years,

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.720
which is more than
ten times higher

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.700
than their actual risk
of 1.4 percent.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.420
Rather than disabusing them
of this overestimate,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.700
some suggest physicians
should do the opposite:

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.160
stoke fear in patients

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.980
who "refuse to comply with
medication recommendations"

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.300
by increasing their

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.760
"perceived susceptibility
to fragility fractures"

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.420
as well as their

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.720
"perceived severity of suffering
from a fragility fracture."

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.660
Since emotion can be more
motivating than reason

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.000
and anecdotal evidence
can be more effective

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.380
than evidence-evidence,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.680
a "graphic scenario
of suffering and incapacitation

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.580
after a hip fracture

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.520
will enhance emotional
perception of this threat."

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:49.320
But hip fractures
can indeed be devastating

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.360
and are associated
with a significant risk

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.500
of ensuing death.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.960
So, what about all of the lives
these drugs must be saving?

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.200
Well, only about a quarter of
the deaths following fractures

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.120
may be attributable
to the fracture itself,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.100
so most of the mortality risk

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.380
may just be a consequence
of the comorbidities--

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.540
that is, the other diseases
and poor health status

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.460
of people who tend
to fracture their hips.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.760
So, they might have died anyway
in that same time frame

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.500
even if they hadn't
broken any bones.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.820
This may help explain
why there are no saved lives.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.400
Osteoporosis drug treatments,
particularly bisphosphonates,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.580
fail to significantly reduce
overall mortality.

